## Forum Topics & Threads — Bot API

Session isolation for bot agents: each thread = one conversation context.
Source: core.telegram.org/bots/api

---

## Types

### ForumTopic
| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| message_thread_id | Integer | Unique topic ID |
| name | String | Topic name |
| icon_color | Integer | RGB color |
| icon_custom_emoji_id | String | Optional. Custom emoji icon |
| is_name_implicit | Boolean | Optional. Name auto-generated, should be changed |

### ForumTopicCreated (service message)
| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| name | String | Topic name |
| icon_color | Integer | RGB color |
| icon_custom_emoji_id | String | Optional. Custom emoji |
| is_name_implicit | Boolean | Optional. Auto-named |

### ForumTopicEdited (service message)
| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| name | String | Optional. New name |
| icon_custom_emoji_id | String | Optional. New icon (empty = removed) |

### ForumTopicClosed — no fields
### ForumTopicReopened — no fields
### GeneralForumTopicHidden — no fields
### GeneralForumTopicUnhidden — no fields

### DirectMessagesTopic
| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| topic_id | Integer | Unique ID (up to 52-bit, use int64) |
| user | User | Optional. Topic creator (currently always present) |

### Community
| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| id | Integer | Unique ID (up to 52-bit, use int64) |
| name | String | Community name |

---

## Methods

### createForumTopic
Create topic in forum supergroup or private chat. Returns ForumTopic.
Bot must be admin with can_manage_topics.
| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer/String | Yes | Target chat |
| name | String | Yes | 1-128 chars |
| icon_color | Integer | Optional | RGB. Must be: 0x6FB9F0, 0xFFD67E, 0xCB86DB, 0x8EEE98, 0xFF93B2, or 0xFB6F5F |
| icon_custom_emoji_id | String | Optional | Custom emoji from getForumTopicIconStickers |

### editForumTopic
Edit topic name/icon. Bot must be admin or topic creator. Returns True.
| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer/String | Yes | Target chat |
| message_thread_id | Integer | Yes | Topic ID |
| name | String | Optional | 0-128 chars. Empty = keep current |
| icon_custom_emoji_id | String | Optional | Empty = remove icon |

### closeForumTopic
Close open topic. Admin + can_manage_topics (or creator). Returns True.
| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer/String | Yes | Target chat |
| message_thread_id | Integer | Yes | Topic ID |

### reopenForumTopic
Reopen closed topic. Same permissions as close. Returns True.
| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer/String | Yes | Target chat |
| message_thread_id | Integer | Yes | Topic ID |

### deleteForumTopic
Delete topic and ALL messages. Admin + can_delete_messages. Returns True.
| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer/String | Yes | Target chat |
| message_thread_id | Integer | Yes | Topic ID |

### unpinAllForumTopicMessages
Clear pinned messages in topic. Admin + can_pin_messages. Returns True.
| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer/String | Yes | Target chat |
| message_thread_id | Integer | Yes | Topic ID |

### General Topic Methods
All require admin + can_manage_topics. Returns True.
- editGeneralForumTopic(chat_id, name: 1-128 chars)
- closeGeneralForumTopic(chat_id)
- reopenGeneralForumTopic(chat_id) — auto-unhides if hidden
- hideGeneralForumTopic(chat_id) — auto-closes if open
- unhideGeneralForumTopic(chat_id)
- unpinAllGeneralForumTopicMessages(chat_id)

### getForumTopicIconStickers
Get allowed custom emoji for topic icons. No parameters. Returns Array of Sticker.

---

## Threading in send methods

Every send method accepts message_thread_id (Optional Integer):
"Unique identifier for the target message thread (topic) of a forum;
for forum supergroups and private chats of bots with forum topic mode enabled only"

This means: sendMessage, sendRichMessage, sendRichMessageDraft, sendMessageDraft,
sendPhoto, sendDocument, sendVideo, etc. — all support threading.

## Bot agent pattern: thread = session

1. User sends message → createForumTopic("Session <timestamp>")
2. All model responses go to that thread via message_thread_id
3. When session ends → closeForumTopic
4. Old sessions can be deleted or archived
5. Each thread has its own message history = natural context window

:: ∎
